[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713423181","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103916#issuecomment-2713423181","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103916","id":2713423181,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hu41N","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T09:52:33Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T10:08:15Z","body":"I've just tried with (I'm hoping) an equivalent project in 3.x and this problem doesn't occur so it could be something 4.x specific (@rburing ). I can't remember how much of the CPU particles was ported.\n\nI'll try and double check this though, perhaps there's something specific in this MRP that I'm missing.\n\nUPDATE:\nCan't find any significant differences between the MRP and my 3.x MRP... (but could be something subtle).\n\nThat it's due to the initial emitting flag in the inspector seems like it's just an initial state being wrong, maybe it's to do with process modes. I'll see if I can debug.\n\nYeah it's the `INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS` mode is not getting fired unless it's set to emit in the inspector. So likely something 4.x specific that we need to fix.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713423181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713574220","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103916#issuecomment-2713574220","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103916","id":2713574220,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hvdtM","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T10:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T10:38:01Z","body":"I think I've tracked it down to the line marked below, it looks to have been added during #101911.\nWhether it was previously in 3.x and since deleted I'm not sure yet.\n\nIt unsets the `INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS` that was set in `_refresh_interpolation_state()`, because `emitting` is set to false in the inspector, and then subsequent calls to `_refresh_interpolation_state()` early out because there has been no change to the follow state.\n\n```\n\t\tcase NOTIFICATION_ENTER_TREE: {\n\t\t\tset_process_internal(emitting);\n\n\t\t\t_refresh_interpolation_state();\n\n\t\t\t// ITS THIS LINE, NOT PRESENT IN 3.x\n\t\t\tset_physics_process_internal(emitting && _interpolation_data.interpolated_follow);\n\n\t\t\t// If we are interpolated following, then reset physics interpolation\n\t\t\t// when first appearing. This won't be called by canvas item, as in the\n\t\t\t// following mode, is_physics_interpolated() is actually FALSE.\n\t\t\tif (_interpolation_data.interpolated_follow) {\n\t\t\t\tnotification(NOTIFICATION_RESET_PHYSICS_INTERPOLATION);\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} break;\n\n```\n\nI'll leave this here for @rburing so we can find out where this line was introduced, but it looks fairly easy to fix by removing (unless the non-interpolated version requires it in 4.x or something).\n\nUPDATE:\nI can't see this line immediately in the history for 3.x, and it looks as though `INTERNAL_PHYSICS_PROCESS` is used purely for the interpolation in 4.x so it does look safe to remove. Maybe @rburing remembers why it was there. 🤷\n\nCould have been left from during his testing or something. I'll leave it for @rburing to make PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713574220/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713707402","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103916#issuecomment-2713707402","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103916","id":2713707402,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hv-OK","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T11:04:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T11:04:56Z","body":"@lawnjelly My bad, looks indeed like a leftover which should have been removed when I ported `_refresh_interpolation_state()`. I'll make the PR to clean this up.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713707402/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713951681","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103916#issuecomment-2713951681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103916","id":2713951681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6hw53B","user":{"login":"JanWerder","id":596986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5Njk4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/596986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder","html_url":"https://github.com/JanWerder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JanWerder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-11T12:12:04Z","updated_at":"2025-03-11T12:12:04Z","body":"Thanks for the quick analysis!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2713951681/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]